course: dictionary
lesson: 11597
title: Ghostly words: apparition
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An apparition is a ghost or a strange figure that suddenly appears. You can often work out the meaning from the clues around it. «A pale apparition floated at the window.» Pale, floated and the window all sound spooky, so an apparition here must be something mysterious.
explain: The word looks like appear, and that is a clue too: an apparition is something that appears. The more formal meaning is the sudden appearance of something unexpected. «The sudden apparition of a rainbow after the storm surprised everyone.» Here it is not a ghost at all, just something that appeared without warning.
explain: Always test your meaning. Swap it in: «A pale ghost or strange figure floated at the window.» Does it still make sense? Yes, so you have found the right meaning. Be careful, though: many things people call apparitions are tricks of light, shadows or imagination.
fact: An apparition is a ghost or strange figure that appears suddenly.
fact: In a formal sense, an apparition is the sudden appearance of something unexpected.
fact: Words like «pale» and «at the window» are clues that an apparition is spooky.
fact: Science can often explain apparitions as tricks of light, shadows or imagination.
fact: Apparition is a noun: one apparition, two apparitions.
exercise: «A pale apparition floated past the window at midnight.» What is the apparition here? | A friendly cat, fast asleep | *A ghost or strange figure | A loud bang from the kitchen | A long, cold winter
exercise: «The sudden apparition of a rainbow surprised everyone after the storm.» What does apparition mean here? | A loud argument | A dark, quiet room | A long journey by boat | *The sudden appearance of something unexpected
exercise: Which word in «The apparition vanished into the mist» means disappeared? | mist | *vanished | apparition | into
test: Ruby saw a shadow move on the wall and said it was an apparition. Why might science say it was not a ghost? | *Shadows and tricks of light can look like strange figures | Ghosts are proven by science, so it must be one | Shadows are always friendly and never move | Light cannot make shapes on a wall
test: In «a pale apparition at the window», which words are clues that it is spooky? | *pale and at the window | window only | a and the | apparition only
exam: Which is the best meaning of apparition? | A type of soup made with onions | A long, quiet walk in the park | A loud noise made by a door slamming | *A ghost or strange figure that suddenly appears
